     see ic_launcher_foreground's mipmap variants and README note in this checkpoint's report for
     why a raster source, not hand-authored vector paths, is now the source of truth for the
     full-color icon). Single fill color per the platform's own monochrome-icon convention — the
     system re-tints this at render time, so the fill color here is a placeholder, not the real
     rendered color. Same scale/pivot as the foreground layer's safe-zone framing. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
